        "evidence_contexts": [
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b008",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
            "content_sha256": "90b884665dd6ee49dfa5fee913f093b60d52f116cc3d78195ba9b97803f2cebb",
            "context_id": "ctx_55d21390aec0ff7a7336858a",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "POSITIVE_POS_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "input gate",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_fcdc03178a1ddc209508d444",
            "source_text": "Correspondingly, the gates at time step $t$\nare defined as follows: the input gate is $\\mathbf{I}_t \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times h}$, the forget gate is $\\mathbf{F}_t \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times h}$, and the output gate is $\\mathbf{O}_t \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times h}$.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b005",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
            "content_sha256": "b3c049aeabeabb53e9775b793ce86f1addf8e527937ad51b8a8c2d6dd3fdbcd1",
            "context_id": "ctx_6a19e08d950ca7bef8fb4c89",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_POS_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "input gate",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_677a13b6f66d36d6302a385a",
            "source_text": "### Input Gate, Forget Gate, and Output Gate",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b020",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
            "content_sha256": "5dca5c30d09667c90ed8c7f0378328b9f18139891b58d13735d880f3e42c7028",
            "context_id": "ctx_6c0d6d0d558005aaf9be6fc3",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "input gate",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_d9eab84c98c32b0f1e563a2d",
            "source_text": "If the forget gate is always approximately 1 and the input gate is always approximately 0, the past memory cells $\\mathbf{C}_{t-1}$ will be saved over time and passed to the current time step.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b007",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
            "content_sha256": "8786cd0135697b270c7b754861ef2c97fb7f7333492b0c23b14c1d7b01335a01",
            "context_id": "ctx_9ee60265b7c99b18fa9a46f2",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "input gate",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_233f5dae07761e1a4528c1bc",
            "source_text": "![Computing the input gate, the forget gate, and the output gate in an LSTM model.](../img/lstm-0.svg)\n:label:`lstm_0`",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b018",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
            "content_sha256": "b6c117b8b37e9b704e6fbc4f4b730b800b7f0673a3041b285c24e89abc732c85",
            "context_id": "ctx_a7c81a70b68bbf602ecfbeab",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP",
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "input gate",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_5eee1983829a0a9512ac9b20",
            "source_text": "Similarly,\nin LSTMs we have two dedicated gates for such purposes: the input gate $\\mathbf{I}_t$ governs how much we take new data into account via $\\tilde{\\mathbf{C}}_t$ and the forget gate $\\mathbf{F}_t$ addresses how much of the old memory cell content $\\mathbf{C}_{t-1} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n \\times h}$ we retain.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b037",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
            "content_sha256": "f87dae16c4798192b496b3fc0c93b3e30bc95a6ff23a95a4bd14cff3c0fa96e4",
            "context_id": "ctx_b2ecc4429423fc36a19369d3",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "input gate",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_82a449631f50a21335913618",
            "source_text": "```{.python .input}\ndef get_lstm_params(vocab_size, num_hiddens, device):\n    num_inputs = num_outputs = vocab_size\n\n    def normal(shape):\n        return np.random.normal(scale=0.01, size=shape, ctx=device)\n\n    def three():\n        return (normal((num_inputs, num_hiddens)),\n                normal((num_hiddens, num_hiddens)),\n                np.zeros(num_hiddens, ctx=device))\n\n    W_xi, W_hi, b_i = three()  # Input gate parameters\n    W_xf, W_hf, b_f = three()  # Forget gate parameters\n    W_xo, W_ho, b_o = three()  # Output gate parameters\n    W_xc, W_hc, b_c = three()  # Candidate memory cell parameters\n    # Output layer parameters\n    W_hq = normal((num_hiddens, num_outputs))\n    b_q = np.zeros(num_outputs, ctx=device)\n    # Attach gradients\n    params = [W_xi, W_hi, b_i, W_xf, W_hf, b_f, W_xo, W_ho, b_o, W_xc, W_hc,\n              b_c, W_hq, b_q]\n    for param in params:\n        param.attach_grad()\n    return params\n```",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b038",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
            "content_sha256": "3a89755d01def81dfe93e85ab32c15756b167fd48c53ebe335576641d3674de9",
            "context_id": "ctx_d97ae77a3b700998ac63cadd",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "input gate",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_95d3eecd0e190204ceeb33f8",
            "source_text": "```{.python .input}\n#@tab pytorch\ndef get_lstm_params(vocab_size, num_hiddens, device):\n    num_inputs = num_outputs = vocab_size\n\n    def normal(shape):\n        return torch.randn(size=shape, device=device)*0.01\n\n    def three():\n        return (normal((num_inputs, num_hiddens)),\n                normal((num_hiddens, num_hiddens)),\n                d2l.zeros(num_hiddens, device=device))\n\n    W_xi, W_hi, b_i = three()  # Input gate parameters\n    W_xf, W_hf, b_f = three()  # Forget gate parameters\n    W_xo, W_ho, b_o = three()  # Output gate parameters\n    W_xc, W_hc, b_c = three()  # Candidate memory cell parameters\n    # Output layer parameters\n    W_hq = normal((num_hiddens, num_outputs))\n    b_q = d2l.zeros(num_outputs, device=device)\n    # Attach gradients\n    params = [W_xi, W_hi, b_i, W_xf, W_hf, b_f, W_xo, W_ho, b_o, W_xc, W_hc,\n              b_c, W_hq, b_q]\n    for param in params:\n        param.requires_grad_(True)\n    return params\n```",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern_lstm_b004",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_modern",
