            "sentence_id": "sentence_c9db3344d8ec2f49dd7abe18",
            "source_text": "As we increase the amount of data,\nthe probability that the fraction of heads\nwill deviate significantly from $\\frac{1}{2}$ diminishes,\nand our training error would come to match the generalization error.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons_underfit_overfit_b008",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons",
            "content_sha256": "86f59202abe22ffd36cd14d8b24bce9d3634dfaee794d959ea21c7f8b01e6ab4",
            "context_id": "ctx_584bed2e44864afc9655baf9",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "generalization error",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_c168df259600cb7c5808e729",
            "source_text": "The *training error* is the error of our model\nas calculated on the training dataset,\nwhile *generalization error* is the expectation of our model's error\nwere we to apply it to an infinite stream of additional data examples\ndrawn from the same underlying data distribution as our original sample.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons_underfit_overfit_b009",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons",
            "content_sha256": "42915dc0aba538a1dbc7e8b734780eb0b3399c937c29289e120c437cf43404b6",
            "context_id": "ctx_7edf6686ee0adbdd3a986dfc",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "generalization error",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_051d24a8e92aeee7eaee8d2a",
            "source_text": "In practice, we must *estimate* the generalization error\nby applying our model to an independent test set\nconstituted of a random selection of data examples\nthat were withheld from our training set.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons_underfit_overfit_b012",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons",
            "content_sha256": "2357fde3ae6e611084b7ca2e590261460b728e654988fe85fa855a19d374a23b",
            "context_id": "ctx_8cd3de6c9b491391cc9a6104",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "generalization error",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_96ed8159a530167fdc27b845",
            "source_text": "In this case, the model that always predicts class 1\nwill incur an error of $\\frac{1}{3}$,\nconsiderably better than our generalization error.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons_underfit_overfit_b008",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons",
            "content_sha256": "3396b5bf07f54f80e9a1c8ae8d6d34a1834f3b66de62fff1ad467c78292d6b86",
            "context_id": "ctx_b89311738d29fd53e93c2b6b",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_POS_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "generalization error",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_0348ff810a1939b66f208bd7",
            "source_text": "In order to discuss this phenomenon more formally,\nwe need to differentiate between training error and generalization error.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons_underfit_overfit_b009",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons",
            "content_sha256": "df40905187c1fbe519a38cda30c7e58510e47861d4d85c0828bc12cbeba8cb38",
            "context_id": "ctx_bfb4aa499a19b3c234af5b7e",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "generalization error",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_79bb0e474f6da51e792c960e",
            "source_text": "Problematically, we can never calculate the generalization error exactly.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons_underfit_overfit_b007",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons",
